{:edb/db-before-t 232 :edb/db-after-t 233 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533545 50 #inst "2026-10-11T05:58:46.225Z" 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186162020 1038 #edb/ref 17592186407584 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186162021 1038 #edb/ref 17592186407582 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186162021 1038 #edb/ref 17592186407583 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186162021 1038 #edb/ref 17592186407585 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186162652 1068 #edb/ref 17592186161174 13194139533545 17592186045585 false] [17592186162652 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407581 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186162652 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186162652 1071 "Find the orthogonal projection matrix that maps $x ∈ R^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $λ =-4$ of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139533545 17592186045585 false] [17592186162652 1071 "Find the orthogonal projection matrix that maps $x\\in {R}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-4$ of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186162652 1074 "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nMoreover, ${u}_{i}\\cdot {u}_{i}^{T}$ is the projection matrix corresponding to ${u}_{i}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to $\\lambda =-4.$ Computing $A-(-4)I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+4I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}]+4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-2{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖v‖=\\sqrt{5}.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we obtain the normalized eigenvector: \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, the required orthogonal projection matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {u}^{T} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186407551 1043 #edb/ref 17592186407586 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186407551 1043 #edb/ref 17592186407587 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186407551 1043 #edb/ref 17592186407588 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186407551 1043 #edb/ref 17592186407589 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186407551 1043 #edb/ref 17592186407590 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186407551 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186407551 1045 "The Spectral Theorem" 13194139533545 17592186045585 true] [17592186407551 1046 #